WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:47.280
Summer in the Bay of

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:50.520
Islands sees many yachts
visiting from overseas, so

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:54.640
sustoms have their work cut out for them
keeping the country’s coastal border safe.

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:57.720
Today they’re patrolling on 
the new Hawk Five.

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:02.600
It’s a serious vessel, loaded with tech
and can travel at very high speeds.

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:07.880
So on an average
year, there’s somewhere north of 5-600

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:11.120
yachts and various other craft
which head down to this part of the world.

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:14.080
So part of our role is to go out

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:17.320
and make sure that those craft
that are coming this way are compliant.

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:20.960
With the speed
and the capability of the boat, we do have

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:24.120
now the ability to react pretty sharpish.

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:28.360
Before long, supervising Customs
Officer Nick, and his crew

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:31.800
get a heads up from Coastguard
that a catamaran may have tried

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:34.440
to sail in
to New Zealand waters under the radar.

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:39.400
So there’s a vessel down
in the Great Mercs

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:42.880
which we’ve been tasked to go
and take a look at.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.600
Got some concerns
around the persons on board

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:48.200
and why they’re here in New Zealand,
and how they got here.

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:49.280
So probably

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:51.240
about ooh, five

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:53.560
hours away from there at the moment,
maybe a bit less.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:58.400
The Coast Guard have advised Nick
the catamaran has a torn sail

00:05:58.400 --> 00:05:59.640
and limited power.

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:02.680
So there won't be any kind of chase
going on this afternoon.

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:07.640
Last night the sailors on the vessel
radioed Coastguard for a tow to shore.

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:10.840
Due to rough conditions
it didn’t happen, because

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:13.160
authorities couldn’t board safely
to search it.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:18.320
Customs on board the Hawk Five plan
to do the search now, and for good reason.

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:20.400
Yeah Czech nationals.

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:24.520
So one motor, 50% one motor out.

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:28.520
Catamaran’s in the past have been used

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:31.880
for large scale drug importations
around the pacific region.

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:35.720
The vessel that we’re going to now
is a catamaran by all accounts.

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:39.760
We want to go and see who they are
and why they’re here

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:41.200
and what they’re intentions are.

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:44.600
Make sure that they’re not smuggling
drugs, or attempting to smuggle people

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:47.960
or something
to that affect into the country.

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:52.360
Back at Auckland International Mail
Center, it's another hectic day for staff,

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:56.120
checking the 18,000 parcels and letters
that arrive daily.

00:06:56.800 --> 00:07:00.760
Customs Officer Phil has pulled aside
a gift declared as cotton sheets

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:02.240
originating from Malaysia.

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:06.280
Just a little bit of shading through here.

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:09.520
It’s not overly convincing,
it could just be cardboard but we’ll

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:11.400
open it up see what we’ve got.

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:16.440
Inconsistencies are a red flag to Phil so
he’s onto this box like a ton of bricks.

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:20.720
I’ve just noticed something on the box
there “we deliver packages of happiness”

00:07:21.320 --> 00:07:25.080
whatever that is so we’ll open it up
and see what happiness is today.

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:27.840
Pretty roughly packaged.

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:30.880
They say happiness can be found in crisp
new sheets.

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:35.400
It is taped here
which could be something a little unusual.

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:38.200
There’s this tape on here, I don’t know
whether that would be packaged

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:39.520
like that normally.

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:42.160
But these sheets don’t
make Phil very happy at all.

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:46.040
It just looks like a perfectly standard
piece of cardboard.

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:47.480
What I do notice

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:51.240
actually about that is it’s a bit heavy,
so we’ll chuck it on the scales.

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:52.880
252 grams.

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:56.280
That is about heavy, 
I would say, for cardboard.

00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:59.080
Years of experience have taught Phil

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:02.360
heavy cardboard spells trouble.

00:08:02.360 --> 00:08:04.440
Looks to be something in there.

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:08.120
Looks like the packaging buried
within the layers of cardboard.

00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:11.480
And if that's that's a drug
concealment, it's a pretty good one.

